 compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["ZipRecruiter, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $469M market cap on $449M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -21% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 89% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $10M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 21.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 613% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.125500708691478},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median 